## 4. Post-Approval Execution Pipeline

When `_execute_approved_invocation()` runs on resume:

```
resume triggered (task_id provided)
  ↓
gate.begin(task.id, channel)
  ↓
_execute_approved_invocation() called for each approved unexecuted
  ↓
  ├─ Bind RunContext(run_id=run_rid)   ← ensures _record_tool uses correct run
  ├─ Find wrapper tool from assistant_agent.tools
  ├─ wrapper.on_invoke_tool(ctx=None, args_json)
  │    ↓
  │    [invoke() closure executes FULL pipeline:]
  │    ├─ needs_user_input check
  │    ├─ user constraint check
  │    ├─ missing_required_fields check
  │    ├─ persistence idempotency
  │    ├─ intent gate
  │    ├─ mutation limit
  │    ├─ readiness / capability gate
  │    ├─ ApprovalGate.check() → returns None (already approved in DB)
  │    ├─ FileScope authorization (P1-B)
  │    ├─ budget check
  │    ├─ convergence check
  │    ├─ network policy (P2)
  │    ├─ dup guard
  │    ├─ write-ahead persistence
  │    ├─ original tool body execution
  │    ├─ mutation outcome analysis
  │    ├─ evidence recording (_record_tool)
  │    └─ epoch / verification tracking
  │
  ├─ _record_tool(tool_name, arguments, TOOL_EXECUTED, result)
  ├─ mark_approval_executed(approval_id)  ← exactly-once
  └─ add_event(run_rid, "approval.executed", ...)
  ↓
[RunContext restored]
  ↓
model continues from tool result
```

